cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the preprint below."
title: "A Factor-Two Lower Bound for Complementing Two-Way Deterministic Finite Automata"
authors:
  - family-names: Arif
    given-names: Sudais
    affiliation: Carnegie Mellon University in Qatar
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
url: "https://github.com/SudaisArif/Complementation2DFA_LowerBound2n"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SudaisArif/Complementation2DFA_LowerBound2n"
abstract: >-
  For every n >= 22, a fixed ternary language has exact two-way deterministic
  state complexity n and complement complexity 2n under left-endmarker
  acceptance, with infinite runs rejecting. Under the acceptance-anywhere
  convention of Geffert, Mereghetti, and Pighizzini, the same family has exact
  complexities N and 2N-1 for every N >= 23. The repository contains the
  preprint, complete LaTeX source, and finite verification programs.
keywords:
  - two-way deterministic finite automata
  - complementation
  - state complexity
  - lower bounds
  - automata theory
